these in the worst case

that ℓ= w = L. Decryption requires the computation of two pairings, as
opposed to ℓ+ 1 of these

for the \emph{Wa}-\emph{WIBE} and \emph{BB}-\emph{WIBE} schemes. We
prove the security of the \emph{BBG}-\emph{WIBE} scheme in

the selective-identity model by reducing to the security of the
\emph{BBG}-\emph{HIBE} scheme that is recalled in

Appendix B, rather than to the underlying decisional L-BDHI assumption
directly.

