Proof: The proof of Theorem 6.2 is almost identical to the proof given
for Theorem 5.1. We present it

here for completeness. As before we assume that there exist an adversary
A that breaks the IND-sWID-

CPA-security of the \emph{BBG}-\emph{WIBE} scheme and then we show how
to efficiently build another adversary

B that, using A as a black box, manages to break the IND-sID-CPAsecurity
of the \emph{BBG}-\emph{HIBE} scheme.

Algorithm B begins by running A to obtain a challenge pattern P∗= (P∗1,
. . . , P ∗ℓ∗). Define a projection

