\begin{quote}
We will also make liberal use of an `encoding function' Encode. For a
WIBE scheme with identity
\end{quote}

space \emph{ID}L, this function will have different actions depending on
its input. We assume that \emph{ID}

contains at least two different elements; for simplicity we assume that
\{0, 1\} ⊆\emph{ID}. For any identity

ID = (ID1, . . . , IDℓ) ∈\emph{ID}≤L, we define

